# Project configuration headers

HealthNodeConfig.h groups the manually adjustable settings for the single
heltec_v4_companion_radio_ble firmware: buzzer pin and timing, battery reminders,
motion polling, environmental cache timing, button acknowledgement, post-fall
warnings, compiled channel defaults and delivery retry limits.

Rebuild the firmware after editing these constants. Detector thresholds and
sequence timing live separately in
examples/companion_radio/health/MotionRule.h (FallDetectionConfig).

The runtime command set fall.channel overrides the compiled destination for new
incidents and saves it across reboot. Existing incidents keep their captured
channel. Changing a compiled default does not override a saved selection.

See ../README.md and ../docs/cli_commands.md for setup and command syntax;
../docs/gy521_sensor.md and ../docs/message_delivery_changes.md explain tuning.
